      "shared_perspectives": "Across the spectrum German outlets converge on the assessment that the Bundeswehr requires a rapid, comprehensive modernization—particularly in digital and cyber capabilities—to meet NATO’s 2 percent spending target and to remain operationally credible. They also uniformly stress that any increase in defence spending must be tied to concrete procurement reforms and a clearer legal framework for arms exports, reflecting both security imperatives and heightened public scrutiny.",
      "controversial_points": "The debate pits a nationalist security agenda against liberal pacifist traditions. Conservatives demand higher NATO spending and rapid rearmament, while left-wing outlets stress budget limits and anti‑militarism. The conscription controversy reveals a clash between civic duty narratives and professional volunteer force models. Arms export reports expose tension between economic interests of the defense industry and ethical concerns over conflict zones."
